70
01:03:33,220 --> 01:03:35,220
No, no, and no.

71
01:03:35,220 --> 01:03:38,220
That's also a pretty good common sense approach.

72
01:03:38,220 --> 01:03:41,820
Just say, look, what I have works fine.

73
01:03:41,820 --> 01:03:45,460
And I can't tell whether you're trying to trick me, so I just don't believe anything

74
01:03:45,460 --> 01:03:46,460
you're saying.

75
01:03:46,460 --> 01:03:47,460
That's reasonable.

76
01:03:47,460 --> 01:03:53,460
Better than being tricked, being duped out of your money.

77
01:03:53,460 --> 01:03:56,460
Or you could, I just do whatever my son says.

78
01:03:56,460 --> 01:04:02,460
I'm still waiting for my parents to get to that.

79
01:04:02,460 --> 01:04:06,460
So anyway, just as it's naive to think that asymmetric information is good for used car

80
01:04:06,460 --> 01:04:09,460
dealers, it actually makes their lives really hard.

81
01:04:09,460 --> 01:04:13,460
Because if you were used car dealer, you wake up every day knowing that people will assume

82
01:04:13,460 --> 01:04:14,460
your lie.

83
01:04:14,460 --> 01:04:19,460
And you have to overcome that somehow, and it's not easy.

84
01:04:19,460 --> 01:04:21,460
Similarly, apply the same model and model to government.

85
01:04:21,460 --> 01:04:25,460
Suppose you've got a great government program, totally passed the cost-benefit test, but

86
01:04:25,460 --> 01:04:30,460
